   "he": "בֵּן, וְלֹא בַּת. תַּנְיָא: אָמַר רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן: בְּדִין הוּא שֶׁתְּהֵא בַּת רְאוּיָה לִהְיוֹת כְּבֵן סוֹרֵר וּמוֹרֶה,",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the penalty for rebelliousness is imposed upon «a son, but not» upon «a daughter. It is taught» in a baraita: «Rabbi Shimon says: It would be reasonable» that «a daughter should be fit to be» treated «like a stubborn and rebellious son,» and to be punished like him if she sins in the same way as he does."
